    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This Introduction reviews literature linking higher BMI, body image discrepancy, and psychological inflexibility (including cognitive fusion) to eating psychopathology, and highlights body appreciation and self-compassion as potential protective factors. The current study aims to clarify the distinct effects of body-image-related cognitive fusion and body appreciation on the relationship between negative body-image perceptions and disordered eating behaviours while controlling for BMI. The section does not mention 'Study 1' or any numbered studies.",
      "evidence_source": "\"The current study aims to enhance recent research on the impact of different (maladaptive and adaptive) emotion regulation processes in eating psychopathology.\" \"Specifically, this study aims to clarify the distinct effects of body image-related cognitive fusion and body appreciation in the relationship between negative perceptions about one's body image and the enactment of disordered eating behaviours, while controlling the effect of BMI.\"",
